      text New in v5.2.0 — Navbar theming is now powered by CSS variables and .navbar-light has been deprecated. CSS variables are applied to .navbar, defaulting to the “light” appearance, and can be overridden with .navbar-dark. warning @176,7602,535,61
      text Navbar themes are easier than ever thanks to Bootstrap’s combination of Sass and CSS variables. The default is our “light navbar” for use with light background colors, but you can also apply data-bs-theme="dark" to the .navbar parent for dark background colors. Then, customize with .bg-* and additional utilities. @176,7675,535,102
